# CODEOWNERS — workflow-change review (OPE-265).
#
# Rationale: this repository is public and its own agents author the PR
# branches. Routing `pull_request` jobs to ephemeral GitHub-hosted runners
# contains outside-fork PRs, but a same-repo branch is indistinguishable from a
# `push`, so runner routing gives a same-repo PR zero protection. The residual
# risk is a prompt-injected agent change to `.github/workflows/**` — for example
# one that adds a `pull_request_target` trigger with repository secrets, or
# widens a `permissions:` block. Human code-owner review is the control that
# closes that path.
#
# `require_code_owner_reviews` is enabled on `main` (OPE-265). CODEOWNERS is read
# from the base branch, so this file takes effect for pull requests opened after
# it merges. The repository owner is the only human maintainer (and the only
# admin), so it is the code owner here.
/.github/workflows/** @qveys

# Own the ownership file itself, so the review requirement cannot be removed by
# a workflow-adjacent change without the same approval.
/.github/CODEOWNERS @qveys
